+<p>The practical workload is broad enough to make specialists useful. In a small survey conducted in 2024 and first published in 2025, respondents highlighted governance, updates, scarce expertise, vulnerability management and notification. Organisational ownership and process worried them more than many individual technical controls. <!-- CHECK: 02-survey-pain --> All seven surveyed manufacturers were large. They already used development lifecycles aligned to IEC 62443-4-1, an industrial-security standard for secure product development. The sample also included five consultancies or partner organisations. <!-- CHECK: 02-survey-sample --> This validates the work type, not willingness among small firms to buy or consultancies to resell it.</p>
