+<p>Each loaded role must supply 1,450 productive hours from 1,880 paid hours, a 77% saleable-utilisation hurdle. Five roles therefore provide 7,250 hours. Delivery uses 92% of that capacity and leaves 594 hours for rework and peaks. The unit costs allocate labour, specialist review and tools. The €334,000 payroll includes unused capacity, leave and training.</p>
+<p>Founder compensation of €105,000 is replacement labour for partner sales, quality and management, not surplus. The €255,200 remainder is pre-tax company surplus for reserves, hiring and investment. Recurring revenue is €691,200, or 76% of total revenue. Concentration matters more: two partners sourcing half the clients can renegotiate rates or move the book.</p>
+<p>The following cash bridge is also a design hurdle. It matches eight year-one baselines and four recurring accounts active for six months. The model delays baseline balances by 45 days, rings-fences 21% value-added tax (VAT), and ignores recoverable input VAT. Other cash costs total €46,000. Payroll is founder replacement cost. Capex buys secure workstations, analysis hosts and storage.</p>
